WEBVTT

00:35:56.490 --> 00:36:00.186
But the ambulance crew asked
if they could just go to sleep.

00:36:00.210 --> 00:36:02.353
That speaks to the culture
of the organization

00:36:02.377 --> 00:36:06.936
in recognizing the stresses of the job.

00:36:06.960 --> 00:36:09.389
AG: The stresses
firefighters endure on the job

00:36:09.413 --> 00:36:12.376
are probably a lot more extreme
than most workplaces.

00:36:12.400 --> 00:36:14.400
But the steps Chris
and his colleagues took

00:36:14.424 --> 00:36:15.582
to support their staff

00:36:15.606 --> 00:36:19.496
still teach us a lot about what all kinds
of organizations can do.

00:36:19.520 --> 00:36:21.856
If you do client service or customer care,

00:36:21.880 --> 00:36:23.355
you want someone on your team

00:36:23.379 --> 00:36:25.976
whose job it is
to care for the caregivers.

00:36:26.361 --> 00:36:27.636
If you do knowledge work,

00:36:27.660 --> 00:36:29.756
you need someone
in the organization to track

00:36:29.780 --> 00:36:31.796
who's getting bombarded with requests,